  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 240 AM Sunday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Frost is not expected tonight. High pressure will \nprovide dry weather with seasonable temperatures through much of the \nweek. \n\nStrong high pressure will be over New England today and tonight. It \nwill extend extend to the south and west to the beyond the \nMississippi River keeping it dry. The pressure gradient between the \nhigh pressure to our north and the coastal low well offshore of \nHatteras will keep breezy to rather windy conditions going today. It \nwill be sunny and cool with highs only 60-65. Winds will remain \naround 5-12 mph tonight. This will keep the nearly surface layer \nmixed and a bit warmer than it would otherwise be under clear skies. \nLows of 38-44 expected. With these readings, frost is not expected. \n\nMonday through most of the week is forecast to be dominated by high \npressure that will be extensive over most of the eastern United \nStates. Low pressure will remain offshore the mid-Atlantic states \nthrough Wednesday or Thursday keeping a dry northerly flow for our \nregion. Highs will range mostly in the mid 60s to lower 70s this \nweek. Lows should be mostly in the 40s.",
